# Dashboard refinements

Codex-authored policy for Phase 28; read AGENTS.md, the active subphase and
archive/implementation-history/plans/phase-28-dashboard-refinements.md.
Phase 28 supersedes Phase26's visible all-runs companions, manual Apply and
manual Load more UI. It authorizes scheduler-owned editable presentation
metadata, outside frozen execution inputs, and operation-specific runs paging
up to 1000 with adaptive batches under the unchanged 240 KiB envelope.

New named preparations require a chosen short_name of 1..35 trimmed Unicode code
points; no implicit truncation for new inputs. Historical migration truncates
without rewriting IDs, immutable payloads, artifact hashes or execution identity.
Manifest v3 is the new named format; preserve accepted frozen v1/v2 replay and
materialization. Read-only Dashboard paths never migrate or rename data.

No selected run means no run card. Selected exact ID means one card, without
page jumps. Attempts use stable per-run ordinal/iteration/authoritative role,
not opaque IDs as titles. Selected IANA zone governs display, not metric math.
Keep unknown coverage visible, explicit sensitive reads, <= 2 active client
reads, cancellation fences, Pause and visibility behavior. Information controls
hide explanations, never actionable errors or incomplete coverage.

Implementation owns only its subphase and docs, not this policy/review skills,
root YAML, real installed scheduler/timer, operator ledger or final acceptance.
